Dear Sir or Madam,

=20

I write to place on the record an operational safeguarding action taken tod=
ay.

=20

At Annex A is the text of an email sent today to the Royal Borough of Kensi=
ngton and Chelsea Adult Social Services, copied to my treating clinical team=
, my general practitioner, the Metropolitan Police Service Safeguarding desk=
 and the Independent Office for Police Conduct. The email seeks substantive =
response on a section 42 Care Act 2014 referral that has been open since 17 =
April 2026 and on which no local authority adult social care contact has yet=
 been made.

=20

I copy this notification to the public record because the institutional sil=
ence pattern that has necessitated the operational safeguarding action is it=
self the matter in issue in the live judicial review, AC-2025-LON-004293.

=20

The judicial review has been at permission stage for five months. Over the =
same period my clinical position has deteriorated, as documented by my treat=
ing clinicians. The relationship between sustained institutional silence and=
 clinical deterioration in vulnerable adults is recognised in safeguarding l=
aw and guidance.

=20

The documentary position is as follows. Since October 2025, twenty-six subs=
tantive submissions have been filed within the judicial review forum. Sixtee=
n remain without substantive determination. In the same period, forty-two su=
bmissions have been filed within the parliamentary forum. Twenty-seven remai=
n without substantive response. The chronologies are on the public archive.

=20

I ask no recipient of this notification to take any specific action. I writ=
e to record, transparently, that the safeguarding action at Annex A has been=
 taken, and that the institutional silence pattern documented in the public =
archive is now formally on the safeguarding record.

=20

Yours faithfully,

=20

Nadia Zahmoul

Litigant in Person

Claimant =E2=80=94 Zahmoul v Secretary of State for Justice & HMCTS

High Court (Administrative Court) | AC-2025-LON-004293

nadia@rosekross.com

+44 7913 328 615

=20

Public archive: https://github.com/nadiazahmoul/Zahmoul-v-SSJ-HMCTS-Public-=
Archive

=20

=E2=80=94=E2=80=94=E2=80=94

Annex A =E2=80=94 text of email sent today to RBKC Adult Social Services and copi=
ed to clinical team, GP, MPS Safeguarding and IOPC.

=20

Dear Sir or Madam,

=20

I write to update an existing safeguarding referral and to formally request=
 information on the section 42 enquiry that should have followed it.

=20

Facts. On 17 April 2026 the Metropolitan Police Service initiated a referra=
l under section 42 of the Care Act 2014. The reference is 0103/17APR26. I re=
ceived notification of the referral by SMS the same day. On 28 April 2026 tw=
o MPS officers attended in person for further interview in connection with t=
he underlying matters. Eighteen days have now passed since the referral was =
opened. I have received no contact from any local authority adult social car=
e team. I have not been allocated a social worker. I have not been notified =
of the outcome of any section 42 enquiry, nor of the timeline within which o=
ne is expected.

=20

Request. Under section 42(2) of the Care Act 2014 the local authority must =
make, or cause to be made, whatever enquiries it thinks necessary to enable =
it to decide whether any action should be taken in the adult=E2=80=99s case and, i=
f so, what and by whom. Statutory Guidance paragraph 14.77 requires that enq=
uiries are proportionate and timely. I am writing to ask: what enquiries hav=
e been made or caused to be made since 17 April 2026; who is the allocated s=
ocial worker; what is the expected timeline for completion of the enquiry; a=
nd what protective steps, if any, have been put in place. I would be gratefu=
l for a substantive response within fourteen days.

=20

Clinical position. I am autistic (NHS-diagnosed by CLAAS, July 2025), with =
chronic PTSD (NHS-diagnosed since 2013), and biopsy-confirmed Sj=C3=B6gren=E2=80=99s i=
n active flare since October 2025 under the specialist care of Dr Omar Shouk=
ry of the Central and North West London NHS Foundation Trust. My clinical po=
sition has deteriorated over the period in which the section 42 referral has=
 been open. The factors causing the deterioration are not idiopathic. They i=
nclude sustained institutional non-engagement across the judicial review for=
um (AC-2025-LON-004293, in which sixteen of twenty-six submissions filed sin=
ce October 2025 remain without substantive determination), the parliamentary=
 forum (in which twenty-seven of forty-two submissions filed in the same per=
iod remain without substantive response), and ministerial channels. The rela=
tionship between sustained institutional silence in the face of documented v=
ulnerability and clinical deterioration in adults at risk is recognised in t=
he safeguarding literature and in Care Act statutory guidance (paragraphs 14=
.13 to 14.17, organisational abuse and neglect).

=20

I would be grateful for an acknowledgement of receipt within forty-eight ho=
urs and a substantive response within fourteen days.

=20

Yours faithfully,

=20

Nadia Zahmoul

=20

Veritas Numquam Perit

Nadia Zahmoul=20


